{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789856030,"nonce":"ioR4fZe5mOQJLFcU/dzPhHWUTwc=","title":"Lua: next with an integer key past the array part does not raise 'invalid key'","message":"The array part trims trailing nils on t[n] = nil, so during a traversal that clears fields the position of the key just visited can be past the array. zl_pos_after treats any integer key past the array as the end of it and continues into the hash part, which keeps such traversals complete but means next({10,20}, 3) returns the first hash entry instead of raising 'invalid key to next' (nextvar.lua 270). A fix needs the array part to keep its size across nil stores (with # finding a border as the reference does) or a traversal marker.","files":null}]}